  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decarbonising Transport in Emerging Economies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transport accounts for a significant share of greenhouse gas emissions in emerging economies. Reducing transport GHG emissions will contribute significantly to reaching the NDCs of emerging economies and the goals of the Paris Agreement. This project developed an evaluation framework for transport emissions tailored to each partner country. The framework allowed to assess the impact of transport mitigation action up to 2050. The project also supported skills development to allow national stakeholders to make use of this framework for  assessing transport policy strategies and reviewing their NDCs with respect to transport. Against the backdrop of climate mitigation goals, SDGs, and the New Urban Agenda, the project also evaluated the feasibility of transport policies on the local level together with the Wuppertal Institute.</narrative>
  </description>
